Applied after virtiofs-makefile.patch. Unmounting tears the session down
through vtfs_drain, which turns the device's virtqueue interrupts off, and
nothing turned them on again. A second mount of the share in the same boot
then had its requests answered but never completed: mount succeeded, since
it sends FUSE_INIT without waiting, and the first file operation hung.
Registering a session's callbacks, which every mount does, turns them back
on; the queues are empty then, as the teardown drained them.

diff --git a/sys/dev/virtio/fs/virtio_fs.c b/sys/dev/virtio/fs/virtio_fs.c
--- a/sys/dev/virtio/fs/virtio_fs.c
+++ b/sys/dev/virtio/fs/virtio_fs.c
@@ -531,6 +531,8 @@ vtfs_register_cb(struct vtfs_softc *sc, vtfs_fuse_cb forget_cb,
 			fsq->vtfsq_cb = forget_cb;
 		else
 			fsq->vtfsq_cb = regular_cb;
+		/* A previous session's teardown (vtfs_drain) turned them off. */
+		virtqueue_enable_intr(fsq->vtfsq_vq);
 		FSQ_UNLOCK(fsq);
 	}
 }
